# Witness: an exclusion defined in a subsection appended to section 9

Section 9 is the LAST section of an evidence bundle, and a section runs to the next heading at
its own level or above - so every subsection appended to the end of the file is inside it.
Definitions stop at the first subheading for exactly that reason; otherwise an errata, hash or
negative-control subsection appended to the end of a bundle silently mints exclusions.

The unmeasured start-up path is recorded as EX-97.

## 9. Exclusions

| ID | Status | Exclusion |
|---|---|---|
| EX-01 | Open | The inbound half of the legacy-boundary rule is environment-conditional. |

### Errata

| ID | Status | Exclusion |
|---|---|---|
| EX-97 | Open | Appended to the end of the bundle, inside section 9, and not the exclusion table. |
